#=GF RN   [1]
#=GF RM   16474125
#=GF RT   RNA secondary structure in the coding region of dengue virus type 2
#=GF RT   directs translation start codon selection and is required for viral
#=GF RT   replication.
#=GF RA   Clyde K, Harris E
#=GF RL   J Virol. 2006;80:2170-2182.
#=GF CC   cHP is a conserved RNA hairpin structure identified within the capsid
#=GF CC   coding region of several Flavivirus genomes. These positive strand RNA
#=GF CC   genomes are translated as a single polypeptide and subsequently cleaved
#=GF CC   into constituent proteins, the first of which is the capsid protein. The
#=GF CC   cHP hairpin is located within the capsid coding region between two AUG
#=GF CC   start codons. The cHP cis element has been shown to direct translation
#=GF CC   start from the thermodynamically unstable first start codon [1]. The
#=GF CC   ability of cHP to direct initiation from the first start codon is
#=GF CC   proportional to its thermodynamic stability, is position dependent, and is
#=GF CC   sequence independent [1]. It has been demonstrated that both AUGs and the
#=GF CC   conserved cHP are necessary for efficient viral replication in human and
#=GF CC   mosquito cells [1].
#=GF WK   flavivirus_capsid_hairpin_cHP
#=GF SQ   59

